## Recipe proof + acceptance review

Prefix every task proof invocation with `RECIPE_TASK_DIR="$(cd ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>" && pwd)"` in the same shell call as the configured recipe command. A separate export does not survive a later shell call. Direct host invocations must use a fresh directory under `.sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>/artifacts/recipe-runs/`; fixed or diagnostic output directories do not select task proof. Independent diagnostics must omit task binding.
Inspect registered criteria with `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" ac list --task-dir ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>"`. Declare their IDs and claims in the recipe's `proofTargets` and bind qualifying assertion nodes through `proves`. Run the recipe through the configured command and inspect its retained results. Recipe execution produces normal verdicts; never set a proven verdict by hand or edit acceptance ledger rows. Retain unresolved results. When the captured completion contract permits human review, present them at the run gate and ask an authorized person for an untestable override with a reason. Without that gate, completion still refuses.
A criterion about the change itself (diff size, revertability, commits, branch, or PR title or labels) gets proof mode `review` and no `proves` node: the code review checks it, and only a new commit clears a review finding. Anything observable in the running product keeps `state`, `visual` or `mixed`.
Inspect the criteria again. When recipe.json exists, render coverage with `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" ac render --task-dir ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>"` to a temporary file, then replace `artifacts/recipe-coverage.md` only after a successful render. Run `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" artifact-check ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>" --contract ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/review/<TASK_ID>/inputs/worker-terminal-contract.json" --terminal complete --require-recipe-coverage-if-recipe --require-acceptance-status` before `mark complete`. Missing ledgers, unrecorded criterion rows and integrity failures refuse completion. Valid selected unresolved verdicts can reach the configured human gate; they do not grant approval. Checked checklist items alone do not assess an AC.

